  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - GPI: Transportation Procurement Specialist, through Jacobsen/Daniels Associates, LLC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This technical advisory services contract provides funding for a transportation procurement specialist(s) to support ongoing and future procurement assistance programs under USTDA&apos;s Global Procurement Initiative: Understanding Best Value (GPI). The transportation procurement specialist(s) will provide technical, sector-specific training to foreign procurement officials on the importance of acquisition planning and understanding the whole-life costs of their investments in the transportation sector. The objective of the training provided by the specialist(s) is to help officials understand how to conduct life-cycle cost analyses and develop objective evaluation criteria to transparently and fairly assess value in large-scale transportation infrastructure tenders, with an emphasis on aviation infrastructure. In essence, the specialist(s) will provide technical training on the sector-specific best practices and methodologies needed to move away from least-cost procurement methods to value-based procurement methods, which may increase opportunities for U.S. companies to bid on and potentially win international transportation tenders.</narrative>
  </description>
